    945  fb32							; PhVcApplyOR / PhVcApplyAND DELETED (2026-10-19) — same retired vcrunch
    946  fb32							; tramp path. PhHcrEntry now stores the prefix mask directly (fixed 10).
    947  fb32							; ==============================================================================
    948  fb32							; ==============================================================================
    949  fb32							; HcrClock — hcrunch animation clock (fixed full=10 since 2026-10-19).
    950  fb32							;   In:  X = full extent (cells, ≥1); reads EnemyRamP (StartFrame-pinned)
    951  fb32							;   Out: A = covered (1..full) — never 0 (always-solid stub)
    952  fb32							;   Clobbers A (X/Y preserved — unlike CrunchClock). No latch: the kill
    953  fb32							;   repeats on contact (DropArm respawns at the room top, so no loop).
    954  fb32							; s = EnemyRamP>>4 (0..15, one 256f period = 16 buckets of 16f):
    955  fb32							;   s 0-3   dwell at home  (eff 0)	  -> n=1, 64f stub
    956  fb32							;   s 4-12  grow to center  (eff s-3)	  -> n 2..full (1..9 cells of
    957  fb32							;	    8px — full=w>>1; w=20 record = center of the screen)
    958  fb32							;   s 13-15 fast retract    (eff 3*(15-s) = 6,3,0) — wipe home in 3
    959  fb32							;	    steps (the old instant far-end turn, stretched to center)
    960  fb32							; covered = 1 + min(eff, full-1). CrunchClock (sc>>2 triangle, ~4f/step)
    961  fb32							; stays for its VCR mirrors + verify_build token gate — only the two
    962  fb32							; hcrunch call sites moved here (16f/step, grow-to-center ruling
    963  fb32							; 2026-10-16). Both callers pass full=10 (PhHcrEntry stages it, HOV
    964  fb32							; tests it); the latch freeze was removed with the 2026-10-19 contract.
    965  fb32							; ==============================================================================
    966  fb32							; PARKED (user 2026-10-28: "HCrunch should stop (retracted) when it kills the player.
    967  fb32							; It keeps moving and killing him again and again", then "still restarts after a
    968  fb32							; while"). LoseLife arms Hover ($FF) and DropArm drops him back to the SAME spot while
    969  fb32							; this clock kept running, so the prefix was extended again on arrival. Two parks:
    970  fb32							;   * Hover set (any death in this room): held retracted until his first thrust;
    971  fb32							;   * EnemyDeadMask b7 = crunch SPENT: a hcrunch kill sets it (.HFkill) and it stays
    972  fb32							;     retracted for the rest of the visit - EnterRoom clears the mask, so the crunch
    973  fb32							;     cycles again the next time he enters the room (or after a game-over reload).
    974  fb32							; Parked = n=1 (clock pinned at 0); the kill test skips while parked too.
    975  fb32				   HcrClock
    976  fb32		       a5 ba		      lda	EnemyDeadMask
    977  fb34		       30 04		      bmi	.hcPark	; spent this visit
    978  fb36		       a5 9c		      lda	Hover
    979  fb38		       f0 07		      beq	.hcLive
    980  fb3a				   .hcPark
    981  fb3a		       a9 00		      lda	#0
    982  fb3c		       85 c2		      sta	EnemyRamP	; clock pinned: resumes at the home dwell
    983  fb3e		       a9 01		      lda	#1
    984  fb40		       60		      rts
    985  fb41				   .hcLive
    986  fb41		       e0 01		      cpx	#1
    987  fb43		       d0 03		      bne	.hcN
    988  fb45		       a9 01		      lda	#1	; full=1: n always 1
    989  fb47		       60		      rts
